description:
Write a miniature I/O manager that calls dispatch routines and checks lesson 2.02's rules, the way Driver Verifier does:

```cpp
using NTSTATUS = std::int32_t;
constexpr NTSTATUS STATUS_SUCCESS = 0, STATUS_PENDING = 0x103;
constexpr NTSTATUS STATUS_INVALID_DEVICE_REQUEST = static_cast<NTSTATUS>(0xC0000010u);
enum Major { IRP_MJ_CREATE = 0, IRP_MJ_CLOSE = 2, IRP_MJ_READ = 3, IRP_MJ_WRITE = 4, IRP_MJ_DEVICE_CONTROL = 14, IRP_MJ_MAXIMUM = 28 };

struct Irp { int major; NTSTATUS status{ 0 }; std::uint64_t information{ 0 }; int completions{ 0 }; bool markedPending{ false }; };
void completeIrp(Irp& irp, NTSTATUS status, std::uint64_t information);    // IoCompleteRequest
void markPending(Irp& irp);                                                 // IoMarkIrpPending

using Dispatch = std::function<NTSTATUS(Irp&)>;
class IoManager
{
public:
    void setDispatch(int major, Dispatch d);
    std::string send(Irp& irp);
};
```

- `completeIrp` stores the status and information and counts a completion; `markPending` sets the flag.
- Majors without a dispatch routine (or outside `0 .. IRP_MJ_MAXIMUM - 1`) are completed with `STATUS_INVALID_DEVICE_REQUEST` and information 0 by the I/O manager itself.
- `send` calls the routine and returns a verdict, checking in this order:
  - `"completed twice"` if completed more than once;
  - if the routine returned `STATUS_PENDING`: `"pending without mark"` if not marked pending, `"pending but completed"` if it was also completed (in this model, pending IRPs are completed later), else `"pending"`;
  - `"not completed"` if not completed;
  - `"status mismatch"` if the returned status differs from the IRP's status;
  - otherwise `"ok"`.

